## Researching the Codebase

- [RESEARCH][!BASE] Begin research by locating the nearest `base_references.md` (directory index); follow the tree to locate the file or concept of interest.

- [RESEARCH][!LEAF] Use the corresponding `.md` leaf node (1:1 per code file) for purpose, responsibilities, and integration points; designed for fast context loading and AI parsing.

- [RESEARCH][!SCOPED] Limit memory usage: do not load all reference docs at once; use the base reference to narrow scope; pull only needed leaf nodes.

- [RESEARCH][!SOURCE-LAST] Defer to source code only when necessary; open the original code file if the doc doesn’t answer your question.

- [RESEARCH][!ARCH] For high-level system/cross-cutting questions, start with `docs/references/architecture_diagram.md` for flow/integration/roles.